		filter: "Responsibilities of Different Corporate Actors ",
		subfilter: " Investor/Fiinancial institutions",
		body: "In situations where the enterprise has a large number of business relationships,  \n7 \nthe NCP recognises   that it may not be feasible to conduct significant research on all companies in the portfolio prior to   each investment. However, in such situations the enterprise is expected to develop a risk based   approach to human rights beyond the mere financial risks. NBIM already takes such an approach to   certain human rights risks, such as child labour. NBIM should build on its experience from focusing   on children’s’ rights to find ways to integrate also other human rights into their risk management   system, provide more information on the processes it uses, and seek opportunities to enhance its   data collection regarding human rights.",
		page: "7",
