		subfilter: " Investor/Fiinancial institutions",
		body: "In the document ‘Due diligence in the financial sector’ (which is not approved by WPRBC), it is stated that   a lack of leverage does not mean that it is not relevant for an enterprise to carry out due diligence. The   document recommends that enterprises carry out due diligence precisely to find out what degree of   leverage they have.6 The document refers to how the OECD Guidelines recognise that there can be   practical limitations on the ability of enterprises to effect change further down the value chain.   Enterprises are nonetheless expected to exercise leverage through inter alia contractual arrangements   and cooperation with other enterprises with which they share a common supplier.7",
