		filter: "State responsibility/Involvement ",
		subfilter: " NCPs Reference to State Regulation/View",
		body: "Unlike Sweden, Norway has also ratified ILO Convention 169 – the Indigenous and Tribal Peoples   Convention. The Convention sets out requirements for conducting consultations in connection with planned   projects in indigenous areas with a view to obtaining the affected parties’ free, prior and informed consent.",
		page: "11",
