		filter: "Host country (Where the Harm Occurred) ",
		subfilter: " France",
		body: 'The French NCP was seized on 17 December 2021 by the Intersyndicale d\'Atos France of a specific   circumstance involving the Atos Group concerning a unilateral decision of 29 October 2021, effective   as of 1 November 2021. The social structure of the Atos France Unité Economique et Sociale ("UES")   is based on a central social and economic committee ("CSEC") and three establishment social and   economic committees ("CSEE"), each of which covers one or more companies in the Atos France   UES. Starting in the first quarter of 2021, the Atos Group has been carrying out a project designed to   develop and simplify the legal and social organisation of Atos France and consisting of reducing the   number of legal entities of Atos in France by integrating these companies, without entailing any   managerial changes. The decision of 1 November 2021 notes the loss of the distinct nature of one of   these establishments (CSEE 3, consisting solely of the company Atos Infogérance) as well as the   abolition of the Economic and Social Committee and the mandates of the employee representatives   reporting to this establishment. This decision has consequences for the representation of the 3,000   employees of Atos Infogérance, with the abolition of around 250 mandates of the representatives who   had been elected by its employees. Atos Infogérance was integrated into CSEE 1 and merged with   Atos Intégration, which became Atos France. This decision has been noted by the Intersyndicale,   which considers it contrary to employees\' freedom of representation and collective bargaining, which   form the basis of the social dialogue provided for in the OECD Guidelines.',
