		body: "With respect to the workplace sexual harassment claims, the parties agreed in the wage and   collective bargaining agreement dated December 21, 2021 that “6. [t]he KNCP shall participate   in the ‘(tentative) Better Workplace for Women project’ to be implemented by the company in   2022” and “8. [t]he company shall announce the internal procedures for reporting and redressing   workplace sexual harassment by January 2022.” \nThe enterprise also confirmed that it had planned and implemented a number of programs,   including training related to the “(tentative) Better Workplace for Women project,” and had   provided opportunities for the complainant, including union members, to participate in the   project. However, there were some discrepancies in perspective between the parties with respect   to the content of the project and the degree of participation. \nWith respect to “announc[ing] the internal procedure for reporting and redressing workplace   sexual harassment,” the KNCP confirmed that the enterprise made the announcement on June   30, 2023 after consulting with the complainant on its content.",
