		subfilter: " Responsibility under Domestic Laws",
		body: "The Guidelines constitute international standards of behavior for multinational companies  \nin relation to general principles, which are not necessarily tied to the national legislation of  \nthe different countries that have subscribed to them. Therefore, it is important to note that  \ncompliance with or contravention of national legislation does not necessarily imply  \ncompliance with or contravention of the Guidelines. There may be situations in which  \ncompanies comply with the law and, at the same time, contravene the principles  \nestablished in the Guidelines and, conversely, situations in which the existence of a  \nviolation of the national legal system does not imply the existence of a violation of the  \nGuidelines.",
