		filter: "Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements ",
		subfilter: " Explanation of OECD Guidelines on Certain Matters",
		body: 'The provisions contained in the Guidelines are not legally enforceable   rules but are "recommendations addressed by governments to   multinational enterprises" \n13 and that while "the Guidelines often go  \nbeyond the law14 , they clearly indicate that "in countries where   domestic laws or regulations conflict with the principles and standards   set out in the Guidelines, enterprises should try to find ways to comply   with these guidelines and standards without infringing their national   laws" \n15 \n. \nThe above is based on the idea that the Guidelines are international   standards of good behaviour for multinational enterprises that relate to   principles of a general nature.',
