		filter: "Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements ",
		subfilter: " Explanation of OECD Guidelines on Certain Matters",
		body: 'Such international rules have a content agreed by states and are (generally)   used as a standard of conduct to which all multinational enterprises must   adhere in their relations or investments in this capacity. \nToday, despite the existence of a large number of tools27 at the international   level that regulate or provide guidelines and policies for good and responsible   corporate behaviour, "the Guidelines [are the only ones that] have the   particularity of including a complaint handling mechanism, whereby individuals   who consider that their human rights have been violated can file a complaint at   a company meeting".28',
