		filter: "Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements ",
		subfilter: " Referred International Convention/Treaty/Other Regulation",
		body: "The UN Guiding Principles,   which inform the OECD Guidelines, explain the ‘responsibility to respect human   rights’ covers a company’s own activities but also requires the company to   ‘prevent or mitigate adverse human rights impacts that are directly linked to   their operations, products or services by their business relationships, even if they   have not contributed to those impacts’.",
